            </note>
            <note corresp="#d737-f2" n="78" xml:id="d737-f2-content">
                <p>
                    Vilhelms Munters.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d737-f3" n="79" xml:id="d737-f3-content">
                <p>August Rei and Fricis Kocins, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d737-f4" n="80" xml:id="d737-f4-content">
                <p>Treaty with Latvia signed at Riga, August 11, 1920; for text see League of
                    Nations Treaty Series, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 195. Treaty
                    with Estonia signed at Dorpat (Tartu, Yuryev), February 2, 1920; for text, see
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >xi</hi>, p. 29.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d737-f5" n="81" xml:id="d737-f5-content">
                <p>Protocol for the Immediate Entry into Force of the Treaty of Paris
                    (Kellogg-Briand Pact) of August 27, 1928, signed by Estonia, Latvia, Poland,
                    Rumania, and the Soviet Union at Moscow, February 9, 1929; for text, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >lxxxix</hi>, p. 369.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d737-f6" n="82" xml:id="d737-f6-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1928v01#pg_153">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1928, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 153</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
